{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1548763-ideas-for-bringing-in-the-gargoyles-bloodline-from-vtm-to-vtr","id":1548763,"title":"Ideas for bringing in the Gargoyles bloodline from vtm to vtr?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-25T10:03:23-08:00","id":1548763,"title":"Ideas for bringing in the Gargoyles bloodline from vtm to vtr?","content":"Does anyone know of any homebrew for bringing in the Gargoyle bloodline from vtm to vtr? Or have any ideas on how to homebrew them in? My idea was to keep it somewhat similar to vtm as them being an artifically made bloodline, perhaps the result of alchemists trying to make a promethean and using vitae instead of Azoth? Or just something the liches made? Any suggestions or ideas stats wise as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-25T10:30:18-08:00","id":1548764,"title":"","content":"There's material for Gargoyles in the STV product <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/395104/Wild-Hunt-Gangrel\" target=\"_blank\">Wild Hunt: Gangrel</a> by None More Dark Publishing, partially previewed <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481563#post1481563\">here</a>, for one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-25T19:59:56-08:00","id":1548777,"title":"","content":"Well, what are you aiming for in the first place? What elements of VtM's Gargoyles you'd like to replay with or desconstruct to take in whole new directions?<br /> <br /> (Partly asking also because &quot;Gargoyle remake&quot; kind of is one of the major recurring subplots and source of drama for one of the PCs of my own current &quot;V20.5&quot; chronicle)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T01:16:51-08:00","id":1548780,"title":"","content":"If OP is going to alchemy and stuff I would suggest a connection, either sympathic or antagonistic, with the Ordo Dracul (possibly making the Dragons take the place of the Tremere in the backstory for the bloodline). I probably wouldn't tie the Gargoyles to the Tremere liches as that kind of crossover would not feel right with me (If it feels right for you, go for it!).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T09:29:31-08:00","id":1548789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1548763-ideas-for-bringing-in-the-gargoyles-bloodline-from-vtm-to-vtr?p=1548777#post1548777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, what are you aiming for in the first place? What elements of VtM's Gargoyles you'd like to replay with or desconstruct to take in whole new directions?<br /> <br /> (Partly asking also because &quot;Gargoyle remake&quot; kind of is one of the major recurring subplots and source of drama for one of the PCs of my own current &quot;V20.5&quot; chronicle)</div> </div> </div> </div>The main aspects being how stone like and inhuman they look and their artificial origins. I always liked how they are basically born vampires either in a lab or from the embrace stripping most of their mortal memories.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1548763-ideas-for-bringing-in-the-gargoyles-bloodline-from-vtm-to-vtr?p=1548780#post1548780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If OP is going to alchemy and stuff I would suggest a connection, either sympathic or antagonistic, with the Ordo Dracul (possibly making the Dragons take the place of the Tremere in the backstory for the bloodline). I probably wouldn't tie the Gargoyles to the Tremere liches as that kind of crossover would not feel right with me (If it feels right for you, go for it!).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T22:07:00-07:00","id":1549994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1548763-ideas-for-bringing-in-the-gargoyles-bloodline-from-vtm-to-vtr?p=1548789#post1548789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The main aspects being how stone like and inhuman they look and their artificial origins. I always liked how they are basically born vampires either in a lab or from the embrace stripping most of their mortal memories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the long hiatus, really struggling with work &amp; life.<br /> <br /> Now speaking of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Annunaku\" target=\"_blank\">stone</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pijavica\" target=\"_blank\">more inhuman, unnatural creation processes</a>, these two while quite different from VtM Gargoyles could make insteresting springboard for ideas - specially if one mixes &amp; matches things, since there's nothing to say an annunaku-analog or <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nhang\" target=\"_blank\">stranger things</a> could not spring from Pijavica strains or vice-versa. The world of Requiem is made of all too many things that die out <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gargoyle_(VTR)\" target=\"_blank\">mostly forgotten</a> only to be later <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Humour\" target=\"_blank\">exhumed</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mandragora\" target=\"_blank\">repurposed</a> or reanimated <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hypatians\" target=\"_blank\">in ways it was not meant to</a>. There's a very large toolbox full of unusual and queer pieces for one to kitbash and adapt to all kinds of bizarre whole new directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-19-2025, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T10:19:06-07:00","id":1550044,"title":"","content":"To be honest I think the basic idea of the Gargoyles, while certainly interesting and valid on itself, is quite easy to bring. In that you're maybe overthinking things.<br /> <br /> Most Bloodlines have extra traits with their own rules. As long as it isn't much more powerful than maybe a 1-dot Merit, or you think the extra Weakness is stingy enough to compensate, you can put the stone skin easy as such a trait. You can add a custom Discipline if you want, and add any other aspects of the Gargoyles as exclusive Devotions.<br /> <br /> You can start out with the Gangrel clan for an easy Bloodline, although any clan will do and in fact <i><b>any</b></i> clan will also do. You can even make them a whole new clan if you want the trouble to figure out and stat a more formal and balanced Weakness.<br /> <br /> What you need for the stone skin is for it to work as the most basic armor (any extra protection should need a Devotion), preferably not cumulative with actual armor. The whole Gargoyle visage only needs description, its effects are self-explanatory (and possible to hide).<br /> <br /> For their creation method, it can be easily folded into the above trait. Just a default rule that their Embraces result in amnesia. This won't by itself affect game balance one way or the other. Then their backstory stays mostly the same, with the Ordo Dracul in the middle, and it's done.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't involve too much other splats in their basic form to avoid cluttering with unnecessary tidbits. The involvement of them is possible, but should be left to the actual chronicle.<br /> <br /> Other than that, the many links <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> gave are excellent for inspiration on means to do <b>more</b> or <b>new</b> things with the basic idea. But the core of it is rather easy to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T15:37:00-08:00","id":1555772,"title":"","content":"In the core book there is a Strix called The Baron, one of the plot hooks involved a childe of that Strix being paralysed but otherwise unharmed. A Strix origin could explain a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}